## Current architecture

### Tier 1 — Wall display and behind-screen pod

The latest hardware design replaces the legacy desk pod and keypad with a detachable wall-mounted display assembly:

- 800×480 HDMI/DSI touch display served by the Raspberry Pi kiosk UI
- Parametric wall rail for 120 mm of height adjustment
- Adjustable tilt from -15° to +45°
- Quick-release dovetail mounting system
- Behind-screen PN532 NFC V3 reader for tap-on-screen authentication
- NodeMCU ESP-32S 38-pin wireless sensor/controller node
- PN532 I²C interface on GPIO 21/22
- Piezo-buzzer output on GPIO 27
- Wi-Fi TCP JSON communication with the Pi on port `8765`

The legacy keypad, desk-wedge, and standalone 3.5-inch TFT touch-pod implementations remain in the repository for compatibility and development reference.

### Tier 2 — Raspberry Pi 5 edge hub

The Pi 5 receives pod events and orchestrates the complete classroom workflow:

- TCP pod receiver on port `8765`
- Kreo Owl 4K USB camera and conference microphone
- Live MJPEG camera stream
- FFmpeg H.264/AAC MP4 and M4A audio recording
- PIL-based multi-page PDF compilation
- Subject-aware session state and automatic handover
- Telegram and Google Drive integration
- Local media storage and offline upload retry
- Principal-led activity reporting
- Full-screen Chromium kiosk operation
- Single-instance locking to prevent camera, TCP, and Telegram conflicts

