## Typical workflow

1. A teacher authenticates with NFC or opens the control interface.
2. The active subject is selected.
3. Optical Scan captures a denoised board image.
4. The image appears on the live projector and is queued for the active subject session.
5. Audio-only or video-and-audio recording begins when required.
6. The teacher can compile a PDF during class or terminate the active context.
7. Subject handover or inactivity triggers automatic PDF compilation and publication.
8. Telegram and Google Drive receive the completed lecture notes and recordings.
9. Students can browse the Telegram archive through `/start` and inline menus.
10. The principal view reports subject, photo, video, audio, and session activity.

